.TH LIBESDM_ES_EXT 3 "2026-10-16" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
libesdm_es_ext \- external entropy sources for the ESDM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <esdm/esdm_es_ext.h>
.PP
.B pkg\-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs esdm_es_ext
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An external entropy source is noise source code that is not part of the ESDM.
It is written once, as a
.B struct esdm_es_ext_plugin
of the header
.IR esdm_es_ext.h ,
and handed to
.BR esdm\-server (8)
in one of two ways:
.TP
.B As a plugin library
A shared library exporting the struct under the name
.B esdm_es_ext_plugin
.RB ( ESDM_ES_EXT_PLUGIN_SYMBOL ).
The ESDM loads it into its own process and calls it directly; it is named
with
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_lib
.I PATH
or the meson option
.BR es_ext_lib_path .
Building such a plugin needs the header only, not this library.
.TP
.B As a provider process
A process of its own that serves the plugin on a UNIX domain socket with the
provider server of this library. The ESDM connects to it; the socket is named
with
.B esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_socket
.I PATH
or the meson option
.BR es_ext_socket_path .
.BR esdm\-es\-ext\-serve (8)
is such a provider for a plugin library, so the same plugin runs either way.
.PP
A plugin in the ESDM runs with the privileges and in the namespaces of the
daemon and takes it down when it crashes; a provider keeps its own privileges,
its own address space and its own life cycle, at the cost of a round trip per
seed.
.SS The plugin
.nf
struct esdm_es_ext_plugin {
	uint32_t version;
	const char *name;
	int (*init)(void **ctx);
	void (*fini)(void *ctx);
	int (*get_entropy)(void *ctx, uint8_t *buf, size_t buflen,
			   uint32_t *entropy_bits);
	int (*selftest)(void *ctx);
};
.fi
.PP
.I version
is
.BR ESDM_ES_EXT_PLUGIN_VERSION .
.I get_entropy
fills all
.I buflen
bytes of
.I buf
and sets
.I *entropy_bits
to the entropy they hold, at most
.IR buflen " * 8,"
returning 0 \- or a negative errno if the source cannot deliver, upon which
the data is discarded. It must not block for long, as a DRNG waits for the
seed it is part of. The other callbacks may be NULL;
.I init
returns the context handed to the others,
.I selftest
checks the source without consuming the data it delivers and runs on the
interval of the ESDM self tests.
.PP
The callbacks are never called concurrently. Both the ESDM and the provider
server call
.I init
before the ESDM drops its privileges and isolates itself, so a device the
source needs is opened there.
.SS Entropy credit
The ESDM credits a block with the entropy the source claims for it, but at
most with what the entropy rate configured for the source allows
.RB ( es_ext_lib_entropy_rate ,
.BR es_ext_socket_entropy_rate ,
or the corresponding
.BR esdm\-server (8)
options). A claim beyond the size of the block is a failure: the block is
discarded, and the source is credited with nothing until it delivers properly
again.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Provider server
.TP
.BI "int esdm_es_ext_server_alloc(const struct esdm_es_ext_plugin *" plugin ", const char *" socket_path ", mode_t " mode ", struct esdm_es_ext_server **" server );
Create the
.B SOCK_SEQPACKET
socket file
.I socket_path
with exactly the access mode
.I mode
\- whatever the umask \- and call the
.I init
callback of
.IR plugin .
A socket file left at the path by an earlier instance is replaced, any other
file is not
.RB ( \-EEXIST ).
The ESDM connects with its privileges dropped (user
.B nobody
by default), so the mode has to let that user connect.
.TP
.BI "int esdm_es_ext_server_run(struct esdm_es_ext_server *" server );
Serve the connected clients, one request after the other, until
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_stop ()
is called. A client that breaks the protocol is disconnected.
.TP
.BI "void esdm_es_ext_server_stop(struct esdm_es_ext_server *" server );
Make
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_run ()
return. Callable from another thread and from a signal handler.
.TP
.BI "void esdm_es_ext_server_free(struct esdm_es_ext_server *" server );
Close the connections, remove the socket file \- the one created, not one
another instance put there meanwhile \- and call the
.I fini
callback of the plugin.
.SS Plugin loader
.TP
.BI "int esdm_es_ext_plugin_load(const char *" path ", struct esdm_es_ext_plugin_handle **" handle ", const struct esdm_es_ext_plugin **" plugin );
Load the plugin library
.I path
and check the plugin it exports, without calling its
.I init
callback \- the plugin is meant for
.BR esdm_es_ext_server_alloc (),
which does. Returns
.B \-ENOENT
for a library that cannot be loaded,
.B \-ENOEXEC
for one exporting no plugin, and
.B \-EPROTO
for a plugin of another version or without
.IR get_entropy .
.TP
.BI "void esdm_es_ext_plugin_unload(struct esdm_es_ext_plugin_handle *" handle );
Unload the library.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The functions returning an int return 0 on success and a negative errno on
failure.
.SH PROTOCOL
The ESDM sends requests on its connection to the provider one at a time; the
provider answers each with exactly one response. Requests and responses are
one
.B SOCK_SEQPACKET
message each, all integers little endian.
.PP
A request is 12 bytes: the magic
.B ESDM_ES_EXT_PROTO_MAGIC
(the bytes "ESEX"), the version
.B ESDM_ES_EXT_PROTO_VERSION
(u16, 1), the type (u16:
.B ESDM_ES_EXT_PROTO_GET_ENTROPY
= 1 or
.B ESDM_ES_EXT_PROTO_SELFTEST
= 2) and the length (u32: the bytes asked for, 1 to
.B ESDM_ES_EXT_PROTO_MAX_DATA
= 512, for GET_ENTROPY; 0 for SELFTEST).
.PP
A response is 16 bytes: magic, version and type as in the request, the status
(s32: 0 or a negative errno) and the entropy of the data (u32, at most 8 times
the length); a GET_ENTROPY answered with status 0 is followed by exactly the
length bytes of data, any other response by nothing.
.PP
A message that breaks any of this ends the connection.
.SH EXAMPLE
A plugin library, built with
.B cc \-shared \-fPIC
and loaded with
.BR "esdm\-server \-\-es_ext_lib /usr/lib/esdm/my_es.so" ,
or served with
.BR "esdm\-es\-ext\-serve \-\-plugin /usr/lib/esdm/my_es.so \-\-socket /run/my\-es.socket" :
.PP
.nf
#include <esdm/esdm_es_ext.h>

static int my_get_entropy(void *ctx, uint8_t *buf, size_t buflen,
			  uint32_t *entropy_bits)
{
	(void)ctx;

	if (read_my_noise_source(buf, buflen))
		return \-EIO;

	/* The entropy assessment of the noise source: 1 bit per byte */
	*entropy_bits = buflen;
	return 0;
}

ESDM_ES_EXT_PLUGIN_EXPORT
const struct esdm_es_ext_plugin esdm_es_ext_plugin = {
	.version = ESDM_ES_EXT_PLUGIN_VERSION,
	.name = "my-noise-source",
	.get_entropy = my_get_entropy,
};
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-es\-ext\-serve (8),
.BR libesdm (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Markus Theil <theil.markus@gmail.com>
